#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/raspberrypios.md:0
msgid ""
"Learn how to install snap on Raspberry Pi OS with APT, reboot your device, "
"install the core snap, and test it with hello-world."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/raspberrypios.md:8
msgid "Install snap on Raspberry Pi OS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/raspberrypios.md:10
msgid ""
"Snap can be installed on a [Raspberry Pi](https://www.raspberrypi.org/) "
"running the latest version of [Raspberry Pi OS](https://www.raspberrypi.org/"
"downloads/raspberry-pi-os/) by opening a terminal and typing a couple of "
"commands."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/raspberrypios.md:13
msgid "Enter the following into the terminal:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/raspberrypios.md:15
msgid ""
"sudo apt update\n"
"sudo apt install snapd\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/raspberrypios.md:19
msgid ""
"You will also need to reboot your device. This can be accomplished from the "
"terminal (and from the desktop), but make sure you save any open documents "
"first:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/raspberrypios.md:21
msgid "sudo reboot\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/raspberrypios.md:25
msgid "After this, install the `core` snap in order to get the latest `snapd`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/raspberrypios.md:27
msgid ""
"$ sudo snap install core\n"
"core 16-2.45.2 from Canonical✓ installed\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/raspberrypios.md:32
msgid ""
"ⓘ  Note: some snaps require new snapd features and will show an error such "
"as `snap \"lxd\" assumes unsupported features\"` during install. You can "
"solve this issue by making sure the core snap is installed (`snap install "
"core`) and it's the latest version (`snap refresh core`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/raspberrypios.md:35
msgid ""
"To test your system, install the [hello-world](https://snapcraft.io/hello-"
"world) snap and make sure it runs correctly:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/raspberrypios.md:37
msgid ""
"$ snap install hello-world\n"
"hello-world 6.3 from Canonical✓ installed\n"
"$ hello-world\n"
"Hello World!\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/raspberrypios.md:44
msgid ""
"Snap is now installed and ready to go!  If you're using a desktop, a great "
"next step is to [install the Snap Store app](https://snapcraft.io/snap-"
"store)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tutorials/install-the-daemon/raspberrypios.md:48
msgid ""
"Snap is an integral part of [Ubuntu Core](https://ubuntu.com/core), which "
"can be installed as the native Raspberry Pi operating system. Ubuntu Core "
"provides more permissive access to the Raspberry Pi, and may enable "
"functionality not easily mirrored when snap is installed from Raspberry Pi "
"OS. A good example of this is low-level access to a Raspberry Pi's GPIO pins."
msgstr ""
